==============================================================================
  2. Universality -- primitive recursion and the mu-operator
==============================================================================
  The mu-recursive functions are the primitive recursive ones
  closed under unbounded minimisation.  LOVA now has each
  ingredient; here is one of each, run.

  zero test    (if-surprise n THEN ELSE)     -> 222, 111   (0 takes ELSE, 5 takes THEN)
  successor    (merge n 1)                   -> 42
  predecessor  (merge n -1)                  -> 42
  primitive recursion  fact(12)             -> 479001600 (matches)

  minimisation (mu-operator) via loop-until:
    mu x. [ x*x >= n ]   -- least x whose square reaches n
    n=0      mu -> 0    expected 0    ok
    n=1      mu -> 1    expected 1    ok
    n=2      mu -> 2    expected 2    ok
    n=9      mu -> 3    expected 3    ok
    n=10     mu -> 4    expected 4    ok
    n=50     mu -> 8    expected 8    ok
    n=1000   mu -> 32   expected 32   ok
    with max_call_depth=4: mu(10000) -> 100 (iteration does not consume call frames)

  Ingredients present: zero test, successor, predecessor,
  composition, primitive recursion, unbounded minimisation.
  That is the standard mu-recursive basis.  Stated as an
  observation about the operator set, not as a proof.

==============================================================================
  3. Ceilings -- non-termination as a structured anomaly
==============================================================================
  Every shape below fails to terminate.  A hang or a Python
  traceback would be a substrate bug; what an AI caller needs
  is the same anomaly schema it already handles.

  unguarded self-recursion                         DepthTrap  recursion-depth-exceeded
                                                              hint: the recursion has no reachable base case, or needs more than...
  recursion whose base case is unreachable         DepthTrap  recursion-depth-exceeded
                                                              hint: the recursion has no reachable base case, or needs more than...
  mutual-shaped recursion through one name         DepthTrap  recursion-depth-exceeded
                                                              hint: the recursion has no reachable base case, or needs more than...
  loop-until with a predicate that never fires     StepTrap   step-limit-exceeded
                                                              hint: the program does not terminate within the substrate step cei...
  loop-until whose step never approaches the predicate StepTrap   step-limit-exceeded
                                                              hint: the program does not terminate within the substrate step cei...

  trapped:           5/5
  full L2 schema:    5/5
  every trap is a BudgetTrap subclass, so one handler covers
  budget overrun, call depth and step ceiling alike.

