==============================================================================
  Experiment 12 -- summary
==============================================================================
  expressiveness:  44/44 cases pass under M9; 0/10 tasks were representable before it
  universality:    mu-operator 7/7, primitive recursion ok
  ceilings:        5/5 runaway shapes trapped, 5/5 with the full L2 schema
  density:         1.19x bytes, Stage-1 0.66x / Stage-2 0.65x LLM tokens vs Python on algorithmic tasks

  NEGATIVE RESULT: on tasks with no built-in shortcut the
  Stage-1 text surface costs MORE LLM tokens than Python.
  See journal/experiment_12.md -- this is the honest
  boundary of the density claim, and it is load-bearing.
